ty mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}(1-p)^{x-1}p, & x=1,2,3,… \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, $X∼\\text{Geom}(0.15),$ so the distribution of $X$ in this case is\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{(0.85)}^{x-1}(0.15), & x=1,2,3,… \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=7) & =f(7) \\\\  & ={(0.85)}^{6}(0.15) \\\\  & ≈0.0566.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360760 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186360300 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360760 #edb/ref 1069 "q-97155" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360760 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360760 #edb/ref 1071 "Given that $X∼\\text{Geom}(0.23),$ compute $P(3<X<7)$ rounded to $4$ decimal places." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360760 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "a90f56db-3bf1-5904-b2af-586397c0fc70" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360760 #edb/ref 1074 "If $X∼\\text{Geom}(p),$ then $X$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}(1-p)^{x-1}p, & x=1,2,3,… \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, $X∼\\text{Geom}(0.23),$ so the distribution of $X$ in this case is\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{(0.77)}^{x-1}(0.23), & x=1,2,3,… \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(3<X<7) & =P(X\\in \\{4,5,6\\}) \\\\  & =P(X=4)+P(X=5)+P(X=6) \\\\  & =f(4)+f(5)+f(6) \\\\  & ={(0.77)}^{3}(0.23)+{(0.77)}^{4}(0.23)+{(0.77)}^{5}(0.23) \\\\  & ≈0.2481.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360845 #edb/ref 1080 "images/31/31519aa878fd6a9b450296552afd9bbf628e30db68a2d7c6dc6b02a48ae28b06.png" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360845 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360845 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "037a7d4f-c46b-5ef5-9f12-e499f543ede1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360849 #edb/ref 1080 "images/a3/a375a537b104f5bcdd8f5951277bce2494d8861a7212772a7d7050fa14091cb9.png" #edb/ref